--TEST--
The two shapes a `static` property has no honest answer for: no initializer on a non-nullable declaration (`E0409`, `rule:classes/definite-property-initialization`'s rule against storage nothing assigns), and `static::$prop`, whose called class PHP resolves at run time and Novis fixes at compile time (`E0499`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Counter {
    // No constructor can discharge this: the storage is the request's, not
    // any instance's, so the declaration is the only place it can be given
    // a value.
    public static int $total;
    public static string $label = "counts";

    public static function read(): string {
        // The slot is resolved where this is written, so `static::` — which
        // PHP re-resolves against the called class — would answer this
        // class's storage for every subclass, silently, rather than the
        // subclass's own.
        return static::$label;
    }
}
echo Counter::read(), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0409]: the static property `$total` has no initializer, and no constructor can give it one
  --> %s:6:23
  |
6 |     public static int $total;
  |                       ^^^^^^ never initialized
  = help: give it a value here (`= 0`), or declare it nullable so it starts each request at `null`

error[E0499]: `static::` does not resolve a static property
   --> %s:14:16
   |
14 |         return static::$label;
   |                ^^^^^^ the called class is only known at run time
   = help: write `self::` for the class this is declared in, or name the class whose storage is meant

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
